# LeakSanitizer suppressions.
#
# Apple's printf family allocates internal scratch for floating-point conversion
# and never releases it, so every "%g" of a hard value (denormals, 1/3, huge
# exponents) shows up as a leak rooted in libsystem_c. Confirmed by reading the
# stacks: frames #0-#8 are malloc -> libsystem_malloc -> libsystem_c -> vsnprintf,
# with our frame appearing only as the caller.
#
# Scoped to the system libraries deliberately. Nothing in src/ is suppressed —
# a leak we own must fail the build.
leak:libsystem_c.dylib
leak:libsystem_malloc.dylib
